GKE is google-hosted managed kuberntes service in the cloud
gke environment consists of multiple machines specifically compute instaces,grouped together to form a cluster 

uniqueness of gke:gke manages all the control plane components for us
it still exposes an IP address to which we send all our kubernetes API requests but gke takes responsibility for provisioning and managing all the control plane infrastructure behind it 
it also eliminates the need of a separate control plane 

node config and management depends on the type of gke mode you use 
with autopilot mode which is recommended GKE manages the underlying infrastructure such as node config , autoscaling ,auto upgrades baseline security config and baseline n/w congig
with standard mode user managed infra including configuring the individual nodes 

autopilot:optimized for production
strong security posture 
promoted operational efficiency 

the gke standard mode has same functionality as autopilot but your responsible for the config , management and optimization of the cluster 
unless you require the specific level of config control offered by gke standard 

kubernetes cluster can be created with kubernetes engine by using google cloud console 
gke clusters can be customized and they support different machine types,no of nodes and n/w settings 


kuberneted provides the mechanisms through which u interact with ur cluster 
kubernetes commands and resources are used to deploy and manage appl perform to deploy and manage appl , perform administration tasks ,set policies and monitor the health of deployed workloads 

advanced cluster management features:
gc load balancing for compute engine instances 
Node pools to designate subsets of nodes within a cluster
automatic scaling of ur clusters node instance count 
automatic upgrades for ur clusters node s/w
node auto repair to maintain node health n availability
logging and monitoring with gc observability

to start up kubernetes on a cluster in GKE we run : gcloud container cluster create k1


